A||N||25||rigdonhome||Fiero Posi Units||||5||
Z||000000||rigdonhome||10-26-2001||11:14 AM||||I hear that aftermarked posi units for the Fiero run almost $1000...  Did any stock Fiero's come with a posi?<P>My '88 GT acts like it has a posi in it...  never spins only one tire, always both.  But a buddy told me they never came from the factory with posi's...  <P>Does anyone know the code I would look for on the build sticker to find out what gears and/or posi it has?<P>------------------<BR>Scott Rigdon<BR>1988 Fiero GT, Black, 5-speed<BR>38,000 Original Miles!<BR>Web Site:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/</A> <BR>Story of buying my Fiero:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/rear_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||10-26-2001||11:28 AM||||Nope. None came with a posi. <BR>The reason that both sides spin is probably because there is no side-to-side twisting motion to unload the right side wheel like you'd have with a conventional drivetrain and rear end. If both Fiero rear wheels have equal traction, they'll probably both spin (or not).<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Master_Sushi||10-26-2001||11:45 AM||||Most if not all of the time when in a corner and accelerating, the inside tire will spin before the outside ever will. I never raced a Fiero before, but this is what I have noticed on the streets. I'm sure a few people on here that race would be able to explain better then I ever could.<P>My 88 coupe was great in the snow though. It allways seemed to get both wheels to spin if I got boged down in snow. I never had just one wheel spining.||||reg||1
Z||000003||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-26-2001||01:33 PM||||same here, I dont think I ever had only "one" wheel spin..<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||10-26-2001||01:50 PM||||Stiffen up the suspension and corner hard. You will get the old one wheel to spin.<P>The last autocross I was at I would have given anything for a limited slip. There was a switchback where the car would light up the inside rear tire. Worth a good second of my time.<P>LSD's tend to run $1500.<P>To give you an idea of what can happen with traction (ie  LSD). In the same place at the autocross  our 911 with a  60 % LSD was lifting the 1 front wheel 12" ...yes 12" in the air. Car hooks sooo much harder with a limited slip.<P>I know the datsun Z car guys in our club scrounge the wrecking yard for Nissan trucks with LSD's in them.<P>I even sometimes get both wheels to spin , depends on pavement though. Right now the 235/ 17's on my car (R compound) won't even spin if I drop the clutch at 3500 rpm , just hooks up hard.<P>Too bad LSD's are hard to find for a fiero.  This is a major must do when I swap in a more powerful motor.<P>Olds Achieva SVX's had them. I believe forum member "cadero2Dmax" (George ryan) paid in the neighbourhood of 3 grand for his <P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||10-26-2001||01:53 PM||||just weld a plate to the spider gears in the stock diff.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> did that o my corvette, my frineds, Corolla GTS, a miata, and2 civics. turns like ass for daily driving but hooks up like crazy!   <P>------------------<BR>0-60 in 4.91<P> <A HREF="http://www.1fst2m6.com" TARGET=_blank>www.1fst2m6.com</A>  - underconstruction - but check it out anywho...||||reg||1
Z||000006||Slammed Fiero||10-26-2001||02:54 PM||||Doh<p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 10-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Slammed Fiero||10-26-2001||02:54 PM||||yah but how much power will that hold up to?<BR>If you put it behind a 3.8SC ..how long before it went boom?<P><BR>Find a diff for your car yet 1FST?<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Rick 88||10-26-2001||08:53 PM||||Phantom Grip makes a limited slip unit that I have seen installed in a number of import and Focus manual transaxles. Maybe this could be used in a Fiero application. Check out the July 2001 issue of "Sport Compact Car" for an article on this unit. Anyone have any experience with this?<P>Rick 88||||reg||3
Z||000009||artherd||10-27-2001||03:08 AM||||There needs to be a better way, I light up the inside tyre a bit now, I'm afraid of what is going to happen with the Northstar car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Note that this is in turns only (which are pretty  aplicable to a mid-engine sportscar....)   in a straight line I will roast both of them every time.   Well, 'roast' for under a second, and only after a clutch dump at around 5500..... (yeah, now you know why I throw so many rods  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Phantom Grip looks intresting, I will have to bust open a Getrag and shoehorn one in one way or another.<P>I am still pondering team Python's expierence with a Gleson "Torsen" unit (that they exploded...)  a v8 with soft compound slicks in a mid engine car is going to put a little more strain that a 3.4TDC did onto a front drive chassis...<BR>But did they get a bum unit, or is the worm-gear accell/decell setup just unable to take such use in the size they enginered?<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000010||skitime||10-27-2001||09:48 AM||||I met a guy at the PA BBQ last month that has a 400 HP chevy engine with a archie kit in his Fiero GT. I don't remember his name. He also has NOS which gives the engine 200 HP boost or six hundred horses. He had trouble with blowing transmissions until he had a guy build him a posi-traction unit for it and since then he hasn't blown a transmission. No, I don't know where he got the posi-traction unit but he said it cost him $400. I don't know if he is on the forum but I don't think so. <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Joe Torma||10-27-2001||10:47 AM||||I've already contacted PhantomGrip.  They said they have 1 unit in a Fiero already.  I asked about custom ones, if they didn't have an apllication for us...I offered a diff unit(I have a spare) for them to mess with...they said:<P>Hey Joe, we have made a unit in the past for the fiero. i will look up to see <BR>what year it was and what part #. if we dont have that info you can send your <BR>stock diff and we will make fitment . the cost would be no more than $399.00. <P>thank you<BR>phantom grip!<P>Not bad! <P>Ski...I wonder if this is the one!<P>If I continue to have problems getting into second, the trans my have to come apart...good time for an upgrade!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">   <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 10-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||skitime||10-27-2001||04:12 PM||||Joe - I think the price is too much of a coincedence to not be the same one.  For that price you should go for it and let me know how it works.  <P>Hey Joe,  You should join us next weekend for the cruise and meeting and food.  If you can that would be great.  <p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 10-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||artherd||10-28-2001||01:00 AM||||Hrm.... $400 both....  Joe, let us know how you make out.  If it will fit the Getrag 5-speed, I'll order three!!<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000014||Joe Torma||10-28-2001||02:12 AM||||I have the 4speed...it will be interesting to see what the previous application was.<P>I'll have to gather some $$$ and when I do get it...the courage to take my transaxle apart.<P>Has anyone work on a transaxle?  I've had them apart, but they have all been bad ones that I didn't have to reassemble. I guess I should replace bearings?<P>I'll keep you updated!||||reg||1
Z||000015||JayUSA77||10-28-2001||02:38 AM||||well guys and joe i just got a email back from them and i will be calling first thing monday(probably to order one) they said they have one for my car(as joe already said 4 speed also) any info i get from my 101 questions ill let joe know and he can let all you guys know. <BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000016||fix||10-28-2001||12:18 PM||||Very cool.  I also emailed Phantom Grip yesterday and recieved a reply in less than an hour.  The reply only said that they do indeed have a unit for the fiero.  I was going to call them monday for more info also, but if someone else is going to call, I might as well save a few bucks on my phone bill.  Let us know what you find out Jay.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Rick 88||10-28-2001||01:00 PM||||Since the transaxle will have to come apart to install the Phantom Grip unit, it would be nice to install a rebuild kit as well. Is there any transmission parts supplier that offers a kit for the Getrag with bearings, synchros, seals, and whatever else is necessary?<P>Rick 88<p>[This message has been edited by Rick 88 (edited 10-28-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000018||Joe Torma||10-28-2001||01:50 PM||||Just got this from Phantomgrip:<P>Joe, phantom grip works in two ways. in cornering and braking our unit works <BR>as a clutch type lsd and it also works as a locker in hard acceleration. <BR>phantom grip is not a full time locker and is completely streetable. we have <BR>had cars testing phantom grips now for over 3 years and 85000 miles, with <BR>hard street and track driving we have had no more than 2% wear( test car <BR>400hp acura integra gs-r)<P>Quick response...on a Sunday too!<BR>Looks like Jay is the 1st guinea pig.<P>I too would like a rebuild kit, for the Muncie..but you need a press and lots of special tools to replace syncros and stuff.  I would not attempt it.  Replacing bearings shouldn't be a big deal though.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 10-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||DreXteR||10-29-2001||01:20 PM||||Hummm.....  Interesting. I get my 5 speed isuzu this week. Does it will fit into it?<P>If some one will email pahntom please ask them for avaibility to the 5 speed isuzu?<P>My pc has been dead for a week, cant send the email.<P><BR>Thanx<P>DreX<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://users.centennialpr.net/drexter/fierofire1.jpg">        <BR>  <BR>Just another Red Fiero - Back 2 the Future Prototype. :D||||reg||1
Z||000020||fix||10-29-2001||03:14 PM||||Drex, I already emailed Phantom Grip about the isuzu 5 speed and I was told that they do indeed have a unit available for us.  They didn't give me any more info than that, but I might call them later and if I find out anything more, I'll post it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000021||artherd||10-30-2001||12:29 AM||||I'm going to be sending them a diff from a 5-Speed Getrag, between us they should have all the bases covered!<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000022||cadero2dmax||10-30-2001||12:35 AM||||I certainly hope you autocrossers out there understand how much a limited slip diffy will add the dreaded understeer.<P>My quad 4 with the Thorsen Gleason pushed like a pig with the LSD. It drove out of the corner fast, but I had a h#@* of a time getting her to turn.<P><P>------------------<BR>G<BR>Daily Driver - <BR>85 SE<BR>4.9 Cad<BR>Isuzu 5 speed<BR>'88 cradle<BR>lowered 2 1/2"<BR>Mr. Mikes interior<P>GRM $2002 Challenge Fiero<BR>84 coupe<BR>4.9 (carburated)<BR>2.86:1 TH-125 w/shift kit||||reg||1
Z||000023||pherder||10-30-2001||09:05 AM||||FYI, <P>Phantom Grip will sell you their LSD but at <B>FULL</B> retail.<P>If you go to <A HREF="http://www.mmrusa.com/phantom1.htm" TARGET=_blank>MMR USA's Site</A> you will find it for $279.95!!<P>Since they only list the 4 cylinder GM cars, which only came with the Isuzu 5 speed (unknown what the 5 speed in the Saturn is but since it is the same part number it must be an Isuzu also!) I would wait until someone sends them in a Getrag/Muncie diff.<P>When Bill's Isuzu Performance got Quaife to build LSD's for the Isuzu 5 speed, he also listed the Getrag/Muncie as having the same diff (along with the T125 automatic) as fitting.  When they came in and people with the Getrag/Muncie found they didn't fit, he refunded their $$$.  I know, I was one.<P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000024||Rick 88||10-30-2001||10:26 AM||||artherd,<P>Keep us posted on what Phantom Grip can do with the Getrag diff. I have a spare Fiero Getrag that I would like to rebuild and install the Phantom Grip into.<P>Rick 88||||reg||1
